     "claim": "GR_busboy",
     "type": "established",
     "claim_text": "An undercover LAPD detective, in a restaurant uniform, posed as a busboy (some reports: a waiter or employee) and collected items Franklin used: napkins, a glass, a fork or silverware, and a partially eaten slice of pizza / leftover pizza crust. A judge later ruled the DNA was lawfully obtained. Headline wording 'and kept a killer's pizza crust': the crust was among the items he collected; Franklin was later convicted of ten murders.",
     "urls": [
      "https://www.nbcnews.com/id/wbna38162451",
